{
  "scope": "Explicit per-reader selected classic RAR4 entry streams: input-derived selected-header spool, native empty-password AES only when R4Salt exists, canonical Huffman tables, 4MiB fresh dictionary, declared-output bound, and no payload CRC wrapper. Ordinary ZIP/TAR/7z and other libarchive readers retain their original paths. Fresh compressed classic-RAR solid selections fail consistently with the native uninitialized window; stored selections bypass that window. The bounded Node RAR4 directory preserves FILE-header order, duplicate names, directories, modern default UTF8 names and the exact SharpCompress Unicode filename decoder and Windows path conversion; catalog construction does not inherit libarchive continuation merging.",
